      "text": "Example: N = 8 with 3 searched elements: 3rd, 4th, and 7th elements. \nWe can use three qubits and we can associate each element with one of basis states:\n\nelement | state                           \n--------------------                         \n1st  ----> |000>       \n2nd  ----> |001>     \n3rd  ----> |010>:marked     \n4th  ----> |011>:marked      \n5th  ----> |100>    \n6th ----> |101>    \n7th  ----> |110>:marked    \n8th  ----> |111>    \n\nWe start with the Quantum State: |u> = ( (1/√2)|0> + (1/√2)|1> ) ⊗ ( (1/√2)|0> + (1/√2)|1> ) ⊗( (1/√2)|0> + (1/√2)|1> )\n\n                                                = [ (1/(2√2)) * |000> + (1/(2√2)) * |001> + (1/(2√2)) * |010> + (1/(2√2)) * |011> +  \n\n                                                  (1/(2√2)) * |100> + (1/(2√2)) * |101> + (1/(2√2)) * |110> + (1/(2√2)) * |111> ]\n\nUnder the impact of searched elements phase flip it becomes:\n\n[ (1/(2√2)) * |000> + (1/(2√2)) * |001> - (1/(2√2)) * |010> - (1/(2√2)) * |011> + (1/(2√2)) * |100> + (1/(2√2)) * |101> - \n(1/(2√2)) * |110> + (1/(2√2)) * |111> ]             \n\n\n\n\nOur measurement results ae probabilistic => You'll get a probabilistic distribution after consecutive measurement(there is\na probability that we measure the correct answer)\n\nExample: |u>= [ (1/(2√2)) * |000> + (1/(2√2)) * |001> + (1/(2√2)) * |010> + (1/(2√2)) * |011> + (1/(2√2)) * |100> + \n                 (1/(2√2)) * |101> + (1/(2√2)) * |110> + (1/(2√2)) * |111> ]\n\n=> We need to     correct states probabilities (thus amplitudes)\n    We need to     incorrect states probabilities (thus amplitudes)\n\n\n-> Create an equal superposition of all quantum basis states\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n->Apply a phase flip oracle of target |y>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-> Apply a diffusion operator:(flips the amplitudes over the mean of all amplitudes)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n*Expression:\n\n->Real numbers {x1, x2,..., xn} => mean= 1/n*(x1+x2+...+xn)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n->Unitary operator: D= 2* |s><s|- I  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n*Constructing D:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n=> This will flip the phase of everything but              state <=> This will flip the phase of only               state => Phase Flip Oracle! \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 50.206889757596386,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Example: N = 8 with 3 searched elements: 3rd, 4th, and 7th elements. \nWe can use three qubits and we can associate each element with one of basis states:\n\nelement | state                           \n--------------------                         \n1st  ----> |000>       \n2nd  ----> |001>     \n3rd  ----> |010>:marked     \n4th  ----> |011>:marked      \n5th  ----> |100>    \n6th ----> |101>    \n7th  ----> |110>:marked    \n8th  ----> |111>    \n\nWe start with the Quantum State: |u> = ( (1/√2)|0> + (1/√2)|1> ) ⊗ ( (1/√2)|0> + (1/√2)|1> ) ⊗( (1/√2)|0> + (1/√2)|1> )\n\n                                                = [ (1/(2√2)) * |000> + (1/(2√2)) * |001> + (1/(2√2)) * |010> + (1/(2√2)) * |011> +  \n\n                                                  (1/(2√2)) * |100> + (1/(2√2)) * |101> + (1/(2√2)) * |110> + (1/(2√2)) * |111> ]\n\nUnder the impact of searched elements phase flip it becomes:\n\n[ (1/(2√2)) * |000> + (1/(2√2)) * |001> - (1/(2√2)) * |010> - (1/(2√2)) * |011> + (1/(2√2)) * |100> + (1/(2√2)) * |101> - \n(1/(2√2)) * |110> + (1/(2√2)) * |111> ]             \n\n\n\n\nOur measurement results ae probabilistic => You'll get a probabilistic distribution after consecutive measurement(there is\na probability that we measure the correct answer)\n\nExample: |u>= [ (1/(2√2)) * |000> + (1/(2√2)) * |001> + (1/(2√2)) * |010> + (1/(2√2)) * |011> + (1/(2√2)) * |100> + \n                 (1/(2√2)) * |101> + (1/(2√2)) * |110> + (1/(2√2)) * |111> ]\n\n=> We need to     correct states probabilities (thus amplitudes)\n    We need to     incorrect states probabilities (thus amplitudes)\n\n\n-> Create an equal superposition of all quantum basis states\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n->Apply a phase flip oracle of target |y>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n-> Apply a diffusion operator:(flips the amplitudes over the mean of all amplitudes)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n*Expression:\n\n->Real numbers {x1, x2,..., xn} => mean= 1/n*(x1+x2+...+xn)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n->Unitary operator: D= 2* |s><s|- I  \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n*Constructing D:\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n=> This will flip the phase of everything but              state <=> This will flip the phase of only               state => Phase Flip Oracle! \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
